NOTE: It's a mod loader, NOT a mod! Install this pack only if another mod requires UE4SS, or if you are making a UE4SS mod.

[size=4][b]What this is[/b][/size]
UE4SS is the mod loader for Permafrost mods. Install this pack if a mod lists it as a requirement.

UE4SS publishes the builds that work with this game only on its [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/experimental-latest]experimental page[/url], which changes every few days and keeps no old files. This pack keeps one build: the official UE4SS zip of build [b]3.0.1-1196[/b] ([font=Courier New]UE4SS_v3.0.1-1196-g236adf26.zip[/font]), byte for byte. The mods that require this pack are tested with it.

[b]This pack is unofficial.[/b] The Permafrost developer does not make, support, or endorse it. The UE4SS team does not endorse this pack either.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
Close the game. Download the main file from the Files tab using Manual download. If you already have UE4SS, follow Update below instead.
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into the [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64[/font] folder inside the game folder, the folder with [font=Courier New]Permafrost-Win64-Shipping.exe[/font]. Not into the top game folder with Permafrost.exe. Full path example for Steam: [font=Courier New]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Permafrost\Permafrost\Binaries\Win64[/font] [i](to find the game folder in Steam: right-click Permafrost > Manage > Browse local files; in Epic Games or GOG Galaxy, open the install folder from the game's settings in the launcher)[/i].[/*]
[/list]

Example after extraction (other game files omitted):
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Permafrost\
├── Permafrost.exe
└── Permafrost\Binaries\Win64\
    ├── Permafrost-Win64-Shipping.exe
    ├── dwmapi.dll
    └── ue4ss\
        ├── UE4SS.dll
        ├── UE4SS-settings.ini
        └── Mods\[/code]
To check the install, start the game: [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\UE4SS.log[/font] appears. Mods go into [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods[/font]. Follow each mod's installation instructions.

[size=4][b]Update[/b][/size]
You already have UE4SS, from an older download or from a mod manager. The zip holds the default [font=Courier New]mods.txt[/font], [font=Courier New]UE4SS-settings.ini[/font], and Blueprint mod load order ([font=Courier New]load_order.txt[/font]), which would replace yours. Keep them:
[list=1]
[*]Close the game. In [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss[/font], copy [font=Courier New]Mods\mods.txt[/font], [font=Courier New]Mods\BPModLoaderMod\load_order.txt[/font], and [font=Courier New]UE4SS-settings.ini[/font] somewhere outside the game folder.[/*]
[*]Extract the zip into [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64[/font], as in Install. When asked, replace the existing files.[/*]
[*]Copy your [font=Courier New]mods.txt[/font] back into [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods[/font], your [font=Courier New]load_order.txt[/font] back into [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\BPModLoaderMod[/font], and your [font=Courier New]UE4SS-settings.ini[/font] back into [font=Courier New]ue4ss[/font], and replace the files from the zip.[/*]
[/list]

Your mods and their settings stay as they are.

[b]Vortex users:[/b] the Permafrost Vortex Extension installs UE4SS by itself, always the newest build, and replaces this one when it sets up the game. With the extension, you get its build, not this one.

[size=4][b]zDEV file (for modders)[/b][/size]
The optional zDEV file is the official zDEV zip of the same build. Players do not need it. It has the same UE4SS, plus the debug symbols ([font=Courier New]UE4SS.pdb[/font]), the developer mods ([font=Courier New]EventViewerMod[/font], [font=Courier New]KismetDebuggerMod[/font], [font=Courier New]ActorDumperMod[/font], [font=Courier New]jsbLuaProfilerMod[/font]), and the UE4SS docs.

Install it with the Update steps. Then add a line [font=Courier New]<Name> : 1[/font] to [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\mods.txt[/font] above the [font=Courier New]Keybinds[/font] line for each developer mod that you want, for example [font=Courier New]EventViewerMod : 1[/font].

[size=4][b]Problems[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]No UE4SS.log after the start.[/b] Check that [font=Courier New]dwmapi.dll[/font] is next to [font=Courier New]Permafrost-Win64-Shipping.exe[/font] in [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64[/font], not next to [font=Courier New]Permafrost.exe[/font]. If the zip made an extra folder, move its contents up into [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64[/font].[/*]
[*][b]My antivirus warns about dwmapi.dll.[/b] This file loads UE4SS. The zip is the official one, byte for byte. See [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-pf/pf-ue4ss-pack#verify-the-download]how to check its SHA-256[/url].[/*]
[*][b]UE4SS.log says Git SHA #1ceefac8, not 1196.[/b] That is correct: build 1196 changed only a Lua file and reuses the UE4SS.dll of commit 1ceefac8.[/*]
[*][b]Mods stopped working after a game update.[/b] Check this page and your mods' pages for updates. To play without mods, follow the Uninstall steps below.[/*]
[*][b]The game does not start.[/b] Follow the Uninstall steps below. Then let your launcher verify the game files (in Steam: Properties > Installed Files > Verify integrity of game files).[/*]
[/list]
Before reporting a game bug to the developer, check whether it still happens without mods.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Close the game. To keep your mods and settings, copy [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods[/font] and [font=Courier New]ue4ss\UE4SS-settings.ini[/font] somewhere outside the game folder.

Delete these from the [font=Courier New]Permafrost\Binaries\Win64[/font] folder inside the game folder:
[code]dwmapi.dll
ue4ss\[/code]
Deleting [font=Courier New]ue4ss[/font] removes all installed mods and their settings. Keep all other files. These steps do not delete your save files.

[size=4][b]Credits and more information[/b][/size]
UE4SS is made by the [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS]UE4SS team[/url] and contributors and is licensed under MIT. The license is in the zip ([font=Courier New]ue4ss\LICENSE[/font]). The components that UE4SS bundles and their licenses are listed [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-pf/pf-ue4ss-pack#credits-and-license]on GitHub[/url].

A newer UE4SS build is not tested with the mods until this pack moves to it. Old versions of this pack stay in the Files tab under old files.

See GitHub for [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-pf/pf-ue4ss-pack#verify-the-download]file verification[/url], [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-pf/pf-ue4ss-pack#why-this-build]why this build[/url], and [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-pf/pf-ue4ss-pack#test-record]test results[/url].
